## Method

- `python3 -I /tmp/opencode/l2u2-thai/extract.py .` writes every (English, Thai) pair of the 8 staged files and of the 8 unit 1 files to pair files. The writer read every pair of each week against the approved English.
- `analyze.py` compares the unit 2 Thai with the unit 1 Thai: the same English line with a different Thai (12 lines), a Latin letter glued to a Thai letter (7 lines), a bilingual line with no Thai character (2 lines), and the Thai glosses in parentheses that the unit 1 Thai does not use. Its report: `/tmp/opencode/l2u2-thai/analysis-all.txt`.
- Each week gets a patch list (exact old text, new text, expected count). `patch.py` applies it, re-parses the JSON, and asserts that every English value and every non-Thai field is byte-identical (the staged files round-trip byte-identical through `json.dumps(indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)`).
- `week-gate.sh <nn>` runs `STAGE_CHECKS` (capture `t31-stage-w<nn>.txt`), commits the week file alone by path, prints `git show --stat --format= HEAD`, compares the English side of `HEAD~1` and `HEAD` with `en-same.py`, and keeps `git diff HEAD~1 HEAD --word-diff=plain` in `t31-w<nn>-word-diff.txt`.
- Style rules taken from the unit 1 Thai: the question line ends with "ให้ชี้ที่ภาพ"; the A3 practise line is "เขียนกลางอากาศพร้อมครู และพูด /x/ ขณะเขียน"; the A3 retest line is "แล้วพูดเสียงของมัน: /x/"; "Who has ...?" is "ใครมี ..."; a Latin word stays lower case after "พร้อมไหม?"; the row 9 line keeps the period after the sounds.

